        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add grouped Claw schema and read-only add plan",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nImplements the first read-only slice of [RFC #27](https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/27) behind `OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1`:\n\n- Defines the strict grouped Claw v1 schema for one new agent plus its workspace files, packages, MCP servers, and cron jobs.\n- Enforces portable exact SemVer, canonical ClawHub names, cross-platform workspace paths, managed avatars, five-field timezone-qualified cron schedules, pinned package-manager MCP commands, safe spawn environment keys, and HTTPS/loopback remote MCP URLs.\n- Reads local package or standalone sources into a deterministic development snapshot that binds the manifest, package metadata, and every referenced workspace source.\n- Produces a complete read-only add plan with expected state, stable diagnostics, local readiness requirements, and a `planIntegrity` digest that later mutation must bind to explicit consent.\n- Blocks agent, workspace, MCP, cron, and unsafe source collisions instead of merging into an existing agent.\n- Exposes only `openclaw claws inspect <source>` and `openclaw claws add <source> --dry-run`; without the process opt-in, `claws` is absent from registration and help.\n\nThis PR does not mutate config or disk, run package installers, configure MCP, create cron jobs, or persist provenance. Package actions remain explicit blockers until the package-owner lifecycle slice later in the stack.\n\n## Stack\n\n- RFC: [openclaw/rfcs#27](https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/27)\n- This PR: schema, source identity, diagnostics, readiness, and read-only planning\n- Next: [#101755](https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/pull/101755) creates the new agent/workspace and root provenance record\n\n## Validation\n\n```text\npnpm exec vitest run src/claws/schema.test.ts src/claws/schema-conformance.test.ts src/cli/claws-cli.test.ts\n# 48 tests passed\n\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs run --config test/vitest/vitest.e2e.config.ts src/claws/lifecycle.e2e.test.ts\n# 3 lifecycle E2E tests passed\n\npnpm exec oxlint src/claws/schema-portability.ts src/claws/schema-conformance.test.ts \\\n  src/claws/schema.test.ts src/claws/schema.ts src/claws/reader.ts src/claws/lifecycle.ts src/claws/types.ts\n# 0 warnings, 0 errors\n\npnpm tsgo:core\npnpm tsgo:test:src\ngit diff --check\n# passed\n```\n\nThe real CLI E2E proves inspection, an eight-action read-only plan with the two expected deferred package-owner blockers, and fail-closed behavior when add is invoked without `--dry-run`.\n\nCodex review of the final uncommitted patch completed with no actionable findings.",
